  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You call forth death and life in a 10-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range. Each creature of your choice in the area makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 3d6 Necrotic damage on a failure or half as much on a success. Nonmagical plants in the area that aren’t creatures, such as trees and shrubs, wither.</p><p>In addition, one creature of your choice in the area can roll one of its unexpended Hit Point Dice and regain Hit Points equal to the roll plus your spellcasting ability modifier. That die is then expended.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 2, and the number of Hit Point Dice that can be rolled and expended increases by one for each spell slot level above 2. You add your spellcasting ability modifier to the Hit Points regained only once, however many dice are rolled.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-4cPXheMAl8DjapnU\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Bloom</em> gives your spellcasting ability modifier; the creature rolls and spends its Hit Point Dice from its own sheet and adds the result.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
